			"widgets_values":[
				"For the target video, at 0.00 seconds into the target video, <Picture 1> (from [Shot 1]) is fully referenced.\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] A five-second handcrafted claymation fantasy in a vertical 9:16 frame begins from the exact character, costume, oversized brown mushroom hat, glowing crystal wand, moss-covered miniature forest, luminous mushrooms, flowers, stones, soft lighting, and centered composition established by <Picture 1>. The camera performs a very slow small-amplitude push-in toward the mushroom girl while preserving her chibi facial proportions and tactile clay textures. A gentle breeze creates slight delayed movement in the hat brim, hair tips, cape knot, grass, and tiny flowers. She blinks once, lowers her gaze toward the wand, then subtly raises it a few centimeters with both hands. The purple crystal gradually brightens and releases three tiny violet-gold light motes that spiral upward around her face. Her blue eyes follow the motes before she lifts her gaze back toward the camera, the corners of her mouth forming a restrained, curious smile. The surrounding mushrooms answer with a soft sequential pulse of warm light, and the shot settles on her calm expression and steadily glowing wand without changing her identity, outfit, props, or environment.\n\noverall_soundscape: A quiet miniature-forest ambience carries soft grass rustling, delicate flower and fabric movement, one faint crystal chime as the wand brightens, and tiny shimmering tones synchronized with the rising light motes.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: A sparse celesta melody at a slow tempo with soft sustained pads, gently swelling as the mushrooms illuminate and fading on the final held frame."
